aluminum-containing adjuvants.</article-title><source>Vaccine</source><volume>21</volume><fpage>3011</fpage><lpage>3018</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12798645</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001044-Lindblad1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lindblad</surname><given-names>EB</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Aluminium compounds for use in vaccines.</article-title><source>Immunol Cell Biol</source><volume>82</volume><fpage>497</fpage><lpage>505</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15479435</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001044-Dempsey1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dempsey</surname><given-names>PW</given-names></name><name><surname>Allison</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Akkaraju</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Goodnow</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name><name><surname>Fearon</surname><given-names>DT</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>C3d of complement as a molecular adjuvant: bridging innate and acquired immunity.</article-title><source>Science</source><volume>271</volume><fpage>348</fpage><lpage>350</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8553069</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001044-Gorse1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gorse</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Keitel</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Keyserling</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>DN</given-names></name><name><surname>Lock</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Immunogenicity and tolerance of ascending doses of a recombinant protective antigen (rPA102) anthrax vaccine: